WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.714
Each of these dangers ends the same way:

2
00:00:02.714 --> 00:00:07.125
a leaver whose access isn't really
gone, or a record that says it is.

3
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:11.152
The quietest are the callback
problems: no callback on failure,

4
00:00:11.152 --> 00:00:15.025
a callback that claims success,
or one sent to the wrong cloud.

5
00:00:15.025 --> 00:00:17.872
Others are about trust: a forged payload,

6
00:00:17.872 --> 00:00:22.100
a broad permission, or a
bearer-token extension left behind.

7
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.798
And some are about order:
doing the work twice,

8
00:00:24.798 --> 00:00:28.225
or running the custom task
before the account is blocked.

9
00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:33.600
Notice the pattern again: each guard is a
lint rule or a check that runs every time.
